Call the struct's constructor to create a value. You can supply arguments
by position or name the fields you want to set.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    Player = | name String, score I32 = 0 |

    newcomer = Player("Priya")
    leader = Player(name = "Rob", score = 10)
    high_score = leader.score
]

The first call supplies the name by position and leaves the score at its
default of zero. The second names both arguments.
Use a dot to read a field, as in the last line, where `high_score` gets 10.

To change a field, start with a mutable binding and mark the write with `~`.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    player ~= Player("Priya")
    ~player.score = 10
]
